.TH TENSINFO 1 "2 November 2026" "tenskit @VERSION@" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
tensinfo \- describe what a tensor container holds
.SH SYNOPSIS
.SY tensinfo
.RB [ \-t | \-\-tensors ]
.RB [ \-\-fold ]
.RB [ \-\-sort ]
.RB [ \-m | \-\-metadata ]
.RB [ \-\-json ]
.RB [ \-\-format
.IR name ]
.RB [ \-\-max\-header\-size
.IR size ]
.RB [ \-\-force\-single\-file ]
.I file
.RI [ key \ ...]
.YS
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B tensinfo
reads a tensor container and says what model it holds.
.I file
is a file or a model directory; a directory is the safetensors weight
set, the same rule as
.BR \%tenspile (1).
.PP
With no options it prints a short overview, one line per item.
A line whose source is missing is left out:
.TP
.B file
The path, the container format, and the size of the tensor data.
.TP
.B model
For GGUF,
.I \%general.architecture
with the name and size label.
For a Hugging Face model,
.I model_type
and
.I \%architectures[0]
from
.IR config.json .
.TP
.B parameters
The parameter count and the number of tensors.
A packed quantization counts its packed values as stored.
.TP
.B dtypes
Each dtype's share of the parameters.
.TP
.B layers
The layer count, hidden size, attention heads (and key-value heads),
context length, and experts, from the GGUF keys or from the
.I config.json
names that metadata-mapping hf_config_to_gguf lists.
.TP
.B vocabulary
The vocabulary size.
.TP
.B quantization
The GGUF block types present, the
.I \%quantization_config
or MLX
.I quantization
method, bits, and group size, or none.
.TP
.B tokenizer
For GGUF,
.IR \%tokenizer.ggml.model ;
a GGUF file without it does not load in llama.cpp.
Otherwise whether
.I tokenizer.json
or
.I tokenizer.model
is beside the weights.
.TP
.B embeddings
Whether the output layer shares the input embedding.
.TP
.B note
Shards and shared storage.
The notes about file layout are in
.B tenspile \-i
and
.BR \-\-json .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-t ", " \-\-tensors
Add the aligned tensor table: name, dtype, shape, bytes, offset, and
parameters, with bytes and parameters scaled.
Shard and detail columns appear when a tensor has them.
Name
.I key
arguments limit the table to those tensors.
.TP
.B \-\-fold
Merge a consecutive numeric name segment in the table:
.I \%model.layers.[0\-29]
is one copy per layer.
A gap stays on its own line.
Implies
.BR \-t .
.TP
.B \-\-sort
Sort the table by name.
Name segments split at dots; a segment of digits sorts by its number,
so
.I layers.2
comes before
.IR layers.10 .
Implies
.BR \-t .
.TP
.BR \-m ", " \-\-metadata
List every metadata key.
Values longer than 120 characters are cut; a cut array gives its item count.
.TP
.B \-\-json
One JSON document: the overview, every metadata key in full, every tensor,
and every note.
.TP
.BI \-\-format " name"
Container to read when the file does not say.
.TP
.BI \-\-max\-header\-size " size"
Safetensors header cap (default 100M).
.TP
.BI \-\-force\-single\-file " path"
Read this
.I .safetensors
file even when
.I config.json
is in the same directory.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show the help.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Show the version.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The file was read.
.TP
.B 1
An error. The message is written to stderr and starts with
.BR "\%tensinfo: " .
.SH EXAMPLES
What a Hugging Face model directory holds:
.PP
.EX
tensinfo model/
.EE
.PP
The tensors of a GGUF file, one line per layer pattern:
.PP
.EX
tensinfo \-t \-\-fold model.gguf
.EE
.PP
Every metadata key, and the whole description for a script:
.PP
.EX
tensinfo \-m model.gguf
tensinfo \-\-json model.safetensors
.EE
.SH FILES
.TP
.I config.json
Beside the file or in the directory.
The model, layer, and vocabulary lines read it for a Hugging Face model,
and the quantization line reads
.I \%quantization_config
or
.IR quantization .
.SH AUTHOR
Nick Reynolds (goldnode)
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR \%tenspile (1),
.BR \%tensdiff (1),
.BR \%tensconv (1),
.BR \%tensquant (1)
